preConditionHook:
// EL: topTail0 = high - maxlist(open, close), topTail1 = high[1] -
// maxlist(open[1], close[1]), and the mirror below the body for the short
// side. maxlist/minlist select among raw opens and closes -- tick-grid price
// operands, the scope their ACCEPTED row allows -- so plain comparisons stand
// in for them.
//
// The rule is a first DIFFERENCE of tail size rather than a level test, which
// is what separates it from every other tail rule: a run of small but growing
// top tails fires here and fails UpperTailCountInWindow and
// AverageUpperTailFraction, both of which threshold the tail against the bar's
// own range. The strictly-positive term keeps a shaved bar out: 0 > 0 is
// false, so two consecutive shaved tops do not read as growth.
//
// Scratch locals are reset every bar; they are declared locals rather than
// hook-scope doubles so a second placement gets its own prefixed copy.
bodyEdge = open[0];
if (close[0] > bodyEdge) bodyEdge = close[0];
topTail0 = high[0] - bodyEdge;
bodyEdge = open[1];
if (close[1] > bodyEdge) bodyEdge = close[1];
topTail1 = high[1] - bodyEdge;
bodyEdge = open[0];
if (close[0] < bodyEdge) bodyEdge = close[0];
bottomTail0 = bodyEdge - low[0];
bodyEdge = open[1];
if (close[1] < bodyEdge) bodyEdge = close[1];
bottomTail1 = bodyEdge - low[1];
